Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"grace|Tata. TATA. Deedee has a LETTER for you. It is GOLD. She will not let us open it.":"","tom|You licked my mail.":"","rose|A LITTLE.":"","grace|Also the moon is gone. Look. It is supposed to be a full moon. Luna said so. Luna is very upset.":"","tom|...There is no moon.":"","tom|There is no moon, and I have a gold letter. Okay.":"","deedee|Tommy! There you are. Sit. No, stand. Read it. Read it out loud. I have read it eleven times.":"","grace|She let us hold it. For one second. Then she took it back and said, careful, that is wax.":"","tom|\"THE MOON CLUB requests the pleasure of TOM. Tonight, at moonrise. Admit three. Adults only. Dress: your very best.\"":"","grace|ADULTS ONLY? I am basically an adult. I have a YouTube channel. I have a SKINCARE ROUTINE.":"","rose|It smells like a candle. I licked it a little.":"","ellie|Girls. You are staying with me. I brought cards. I cheat. You will learn a great deal.":"","deedee|Forty years I have lived in this town. Every full moon, the lights used to go on in that dome above Luna’s. Nobody I know has ever been invited. Not once.":"","tom|Gold wax seal. A little clock on it.":"","boppy|I am not wearing a tie.":"","boppy|...I am wearing the tie.":"","tom|You went?":"","ellie|Darling, I went to everything. The last dance. A big silver ball turned all night. Then they locked the doors and nobody ever said why.":"","ellie|I left a coat there. Purple velvet. I was in a hurry.":"","deedee|And now the moon is missing. Three nights. I power walk at nine. I walked straight into the Hendersons’ hedge.":"","tom|A missing moon, a locked club, and a little gold clock. Everybody get your shoes.":"","ellie|The Moon Club. I have not heard that name since 1971.":"","luna|Oh! Visitors. At night. Is that... is that an INVITATION?":"","tom|The Moon Club. Tonight. Admit three.":"","deedee|Honey, show her the seal.":"","luna|And my telescope cannot find the moon. It is not behind a cloud. It is not anywhere. It is just GONE.":"","luna|Twelve years I have swept this floor. That little silver door in the back has never once opened. I thought it was a closet.":"","luna|...It was not a closet.":"","deedee|Oh. Oh, Tommy. It is beautiful.":"","boppy|Stairs. Of course it is stairs. Nobody take them fast.":"","deedee|It is FILTHY. Fifty years of dust. Somebody hand me a mop.":"","boppy|Nobody is here. A party and nobody is here.":"","tom|Look at the east window. Moonlight. Just a thread of it.":"","tom|The moon is not gone. Something up in the Dome is pulling all of its light inside. Only a little gets out.":"","deedee|The plaque says MEMBERS ARE ADMITTED BY MOONLIGHT. And look, three little brass stands. Somebody took the mirrors.":"","boppy|A coat check, a card room, a ballroom. Three rooms. Three stands. I count three suspects.":"","boppy|Assistant Deputy Warden. Rikers. I know what a lineup looks like.":"","log|Ticket? Do you have a ticket? I am holding this coat for ticket seven. She said she would be right back.":"","log|That was 1971. I have not let go once. I am VERY good at hanging on.":"","tom|And our mirror is hanging off your other shoulder.":"","log|Nobody gets anything without a ticket.":"","deedee|Okay, everybody up. Deedee is a nurse. Up, up. Little sip of water. Good.":"","log|...Okay. Okay. You can take it to her. Tell her I held on the whole time.":"","tom|A round mirror in a brass frame. It says MIRROR 1 on the back. It goes on a stand in the hall.":"","deedee|We will tell her, honey. She will be so pleased. She will pretend not to be. That is how you know.":"","boppy|Three mirrors. Three stands. One little moonbeam. I did not drive a car for forty years without learning about mirrors.":"","boppy|The mailbox moved.":"","toad|Deal me in. No. Wait. Do not deal me in. You are cheating. Everybody is cheating. The MIRROR is cheating.":"","boppy|Gin rummy with Deedee, fifty years. I have never won a hand. Not one. I know a sore loser when I see one.":"","deedee|You ARE a sore loser, honey.":"","boppy|I am a sore WINNER. Who has not won yet.":"","deedee|Purple velvet. Tommy. That is Aunt Ellie’s coat.":"","boppy|Sunday. My house. Bring your own deck. You will lose. I will lose too. We can lose together.":"","toad|...Best two out of three?":"","deedee|Look at you. Making a friend.":"","tom|A round mirror in a brass frame. It says MIRROR 2 on the back. It goes on a stand in the hall.":"","mudling|Every song, 1924 to 1971. I stood right here. Nobody. Ever.":"","tom|Then we will ask. Nicely. After you give us the mirror.":"","mudling|Oh. Oh no. People. Do not look at me. I am just here. With the wall. And this mirror. Which I am hiding behind.":"","tom|She?":"","deedee|Oh, sweetheart. Nobody asked you to dance, did they?":"","mudling|...You were very nice about it. For a fight. Here. The mirror. It was the big one, over the bandstand, before she came.":"","tom|A round mirror in a brass frame. It says MIRROR 3 on the back. It goes on a stand in the hall.":"","deedee|Fifty-two years, and he still asks. Every time.":"","tom|(Tom does not take a picture. Tom takes four pictures.)":"","deedee|Admitted by moonlight. Oh, I have goosebumps. Tommy, feel my arm.":"","tom|So you took the moon.":"","bigone|I CAUGHT it. All of it. Every bit of moonlight, right here in me.":"","bigone|If I am the brightest thing in the whole sky, somebody will HAVE to come dance. And look. Somebody did.":"","bigone|Then they can come UP. One more dance. Just one. Everybody, under me, forever.":"","boppy|Forever is a lot of dancing. And everybody dances too fast.":"","bigone|Every full moon, they danced under me. Then the last dance. The band said see you next moon. Nobody came back.":"","tom|Deedee, Boppy, behind me. No touching, please.":"","deedee|Up, everybody. Deedee is a nurse.":"","deedee|Honey, there is a whole town walking into hedges down there.":"","bigone|...Fine. The party is over. It was over in 1971. I just did not want to be the one to turn off the lights.":"","deedee|Oh, honey. Nobody has to turn off the lights. We will come back. Every full moon. I will bring crisp.":"","bigone|One dance. Before you go. Somebody. Please.":"","tom|I mostly sway.":"","deedee|Then sway with your mother.":"","deedee|Tommy. Dance with your mother.":"","bigone|Here. One of my little mirrors. For the lady who said she would come back. So you can carry a bit of the moon home.":"","boppy|Something fell out of her top. On the bandstand. Something gold.":"","deedee|Somebody invited you up here, Tommy. Not her. She cannot hold a pen. She is a ball.":"","tom|The sundial. The steamer. The sign-up sheet. My jar. The book from 1952. The oven from 1963. Now a mirrorball from 1971.":"","deedee|Somebody who knew you would come. And that you would bring your mother.":"","tom|Somebody with a little clock. I am adding it to the list.":"","grace|TATA! The MOON came back! We saw it from the window! Aunt Ellie said it was probably you.":"","rose|I won at cards. I cheated. Aunt Ellie said I am a natural.":"","ellie|She is. It is frightening. Well? Was there a ball?":"","deedee|Ellie. There was a BALL. A big silver one. She remembered you. And look what we brought home.":"","ellie|...My coat. Ticket seven.":"","ellie|I left it at the last dance. I was in a hurry. I had a date with a man who turned out to be a disappointment. The coat was not.":"","boppy|I wore the tie. Everybody saw. Nobody can say I did not wear the tie.":"","deedee|Tommy, there was something else in the envelope. Stuck to the bottom. I did not see it. I read it eleven times and I did not see it.":"","ellie|It has not fit me since 1972. Keep it, Tom. Somebody in this family should wear velvet properly.":"","tom|A boarding pass. \"BOARDING GROUP 0. FROM: LONG ISLAND. TO: NOWHERE. GATE: TO BE ANNOUNCED.\" And a little gold clock.":"","tom|There is no boarding group zero. I have flown Delta One forty times. I would know.":"","rose|Can I come? I will be good. I will be medium good.":"","luna|The moon is back. I looked at it for an hour. I did not even write anything down.":"","grace|Tata. Somebody wants you to go on a TRIP.":"","luna|If you see the moon up there, please tell it to come home. My telescope misses it.":"","luna|There is supposed to be a full moon tonight. My telescope cannot find it.":"","luna|It is not behind a cloud. It is just not THERE. I checked four times.":"","ellie|The girls and I are playing cards. I am winning. I am also cheating. They are learning a great deal.":"","ellie|Go. Dance. Somebody in this family should get to finish a party at the Moon Club.":"","luna|The door is open. Twelve years I have swept this floor, and that door is open.":"","ellie|I had a date with a man who turned out to be a disappointment. The coat was not. Keep it warm for me.":"","skeeter|Nobody has come to the door since 1971. I have kept the line VERY tidy.":"","skeeter|Back of the line! Round two!":"","ellie|My coat. Ticket seven. I left it at the last dance and never went back for it.":"","skeeter|Round 2. Still not on the list.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Still not on the list.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Still not on the list.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Still not on the list.":"","skeeter|I hold everyone back. Nobody ever asks to go in with me.":"","skeeter|...name? Your name. It is not here.":"","skeeter|The list. Everybody wants to be on the list.":"","grump|Black tie. Black TIE. Is that a fishing vest? At the Moon Club?":"","grump|Nobody dresses up anymore. Nobody even irons.":"","grump|Round 2. Still starched.":"","grump|Round 3. Still starched.":"","grump|Round 4. Still starched.":"","grump|Hmph! Round two!":"","grump|...one does not RUN in a ballroom.":"","grump|I was ironed in 1971. I have stayed ironed.":"","log|A lady left this coat with me in 1971. She said she would be right back.":"","grump|Round 5. Still starched.":"","log|Hang on! Round two!":"","log|Round 2. Still holding on.":"","log|I have held on for fifty-five years. That is my whole job. Holding on.":"","log|Round 3. Still holding on.":"","log|Round 5. Still holding on.":"","log|Round 4. Still holding on.":"","log|She said she would be right back. 1971.":"","toad|Fifty-five years in this deck. Every game they play, they take me out first.":"","toad|Rematch! Round two!":"","toad|I am wild. WILD. Nobody ever plays me.":"","toad|Round 2. Best 2 out of 2.":"","toad|Round 3. Best 3 out of 3.":"","toad|Round 4. Best 4 out of 4.":"","toad|Round 5. Best 5 out of 5.":"","toad|...rigged. The whole game is RIGGED.":"","toad|Best two out of three. Best three out of five.":"","mudling|Every dance, I stood right here. Every song. Nobody ever asked.":"","mudling|I am not shy. I am just very, very good at walls.":"","mudling|Oh no. Round two.":"","mudling|Round 2. Still against the wall.":"","mudling|Round 3. Still against the wall.":"","mudling|Round 4. Still against the wall.":"","mudling|Round 5. Still against the wall.":"","mudling|...I am fine here. By the wall. With the wall.":"","mudling|Nobody asked me. In 1971. Or since.":"","bigone|Every full moon they danced under me. Then the last dance, and the doors closed.":"","bigone|If I am the brightest thing in the sky, somebody will HAVE to come.":"","bigone|From the top! Round two!":"","bigone|Round 2. The band plays on.":"","bigone|Round 3. The band plays on.":"","bigone|Round 5. The band plays on.":"","bigone|Round 4. The band plays on.":"","log|...ticket seven. I am holding ticket seven.":"","bigone|...one more song. Just one.":"","bigone|They said see you next moon. 1971.":"","amy|Report cards AND a 10K on Saturday. Go. Take Mom and Dad. Make Dad wear the tie.":"","deedee|Not yet, honey. I am still deciding on earrings. Come back with the invitation.":"","boppy|Not yet. I am still looking for the tie. I have one tie.":"","sal|Airport? You just got here. Your mother called the depot. Three times. Something about a letter.":"","sal|She said, and I quote, \"tell him it has a SEAL.\"":"","deedee|You are wearing the tie.":"","rose|I am six. Is six adults?":"","deedee|Admit three, Tommy. You. Me. And Boppy.":"","deedee|You drove into the mailbox twice, honey.":"","mudling|The Mirrorball. Up in the Dome. She has not stopped spinning in three nights.":"","boppy|A slow one. My stomach gets one song. One. Deedee. May I.":"","boppy|Somebody up there is playing music. Very loud music. In 1971 they called that a nuisance.":"","deedee|Tommy. Over the bandstand. It is so BRIGHT. I cannot look at it. I am looking at it.":"","bigone|Guests! GUESTS! Oh, at last. Welcome to the Moon Club. Nobody has come up those stairs since 1971.":"","deedee|Tommy, whatever her shiny side shows bounces right back. Use something else. And honey, nobody has asked her to dance since 1971. Three times.":"","luna|I swept the club stairs. Twelve years of wondering, and it was just a very dusty party.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"grace":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"i4CzbCVWoqvD0P1QJCUL","name":"Ivy","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8}},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"deedee":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"3atomJkX2UWSHPSg86Z0","name":"AoT Deedee (Long Island)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8}},"ellie":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":true,"voice_id":"5nPpmcfu7pDFPztXuQIJ","name":"AoT Aunt Ellie (Long Island)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"desc":"A very elderly woman in her nineties with a grand, theatrical, sharp-witted voice and a refined mid-Atlantic accent. Dry, imperious and glamorous, slow deliberate delivery, every line a bon mot. Clean studio recording."},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"amy":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"R3ZxkaLekDWMqVjuSScJ","name":"AoT Amy (Long Island)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8}},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."}});
